Guava Version
33.3.0-jre
Description
The @CollectionFeature.Require(absent = ...) element is supposed to determine which features should not be enabled. The problem is that for absent it also considers implicit features:



      guava/guava-testlib/src/com/google/common/collect/testing/features/FeatureUtil.java


        Lines 191 to 192
      in
      a3b5188







           Set<Feature<?>> allAbsentFeatures = 




               addImpliedFeatures(Helpers.<Feature<?>>copyToSet(absentFeatures)); 





This is probably wrong, because for absent the direction is the opposite.
For example the feature ALLOWS_NULL_VALUES implies ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES.
And CollectionAddTester#testAdd_nullUnsupported() specifies absent = ALLOWS_NULL_VALUES.
With the current implementation this means if ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES is enabled but ALLOWS_NULL_VALUES is not, then testAdd_nullUnsupported is erroneously not executed, even though it works fine regardless of whether ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES is used. The correct behavior for absent would be to not consider implicit features (or am I overlooking a use case?)1.
This means you cannot test a collection which permits null queries, but disallows null values, because

if you don't use ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES, then null queries are not tested
if you use ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES, then null additions (which should throw) are not tested

Example
AtomicBoolean calledAddNull = new AtomicBoolean(false);
class NonNullList<E> extends AbstractList<E> {
  private final List<E> delegate = new ArrayList<>();

  @Override
  public int size() {
    return delegate.size();
  }

  @Override
  public E get(int index) {
    return delegate.get(index);
  }

  @Override
  public void add(int index, E element) {
    if (element == null) {
      calledAddNull.set(true);
    }
    Objects.requireNonNull(element);
    delegate.add(index, element);
  }
}

Test test = ListTestSuiteBuilder.using(new TestStringListGenerator() {
  @Override
  protected List<String> create(String[] elements) {
    List<String> list = new NonNullList<>();
    list.addAll(Arrays.asList(elements));
    return list;
  }
})
  .withFeatures(
    CollectionSize.ONE,
    // CollectionFeature.ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES,
    CollectionFeature.SUPPORTS_ADD
  )
  .named("NonNullList")
  .createTestSuite();

TestResult testResult = new TestResult();
test.run(testResult);

System.out.println("Called `add(null)`: " + calledAddNull.get());
if (testResult.wasSuccessful()) {
  System.out.println("SUCCESS");
} else {
  System.out.println("ERROR");
  System.out.println("failures: " + Collections.list(testResult.failures()));
  System.out.println("errors: " + Collections.list(testResult.errors()));
}
Run once with ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES enabled, and once with it disabled.
Expected Behavior
In both cases "Called add(null): true" should have been printed
Actual Behavior
When ALLOWS_NULL_QUERIES is enabled, "Called add(null): false" is printed
